From 9cbd4fe2882f4b78a5dcc338b292b6bc64aeec65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 20:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): reuse target and step-0 anchor indexer top-k
 selection in DSpark

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 (patch 0761 head 2756478b60b9)
Rationale: When DSpark draft layers run with indexed attention (compress_ratio > 0, idx_width = 512), scoring the full KPool across all 5 draft query positions per request scales linearly with context length (reaching 2.89 ms/step for 1 shared indexer and 8.30 ms/step for 3 per-layer indexers at 256K c8 on TP=4). Because the target model already scores the accepted anchor position at layer 36 during verification and DSpark sliding-window attention (swa_width = 136) covers all 5 newly drafted tail positions, gathering the target anchor top-k row (or broadcasting step-0 anchor top-k across steps 1..4) eliminates 80%..100% of draft indexer work and keeps indexed draft attention O(1) across 4K..256K.
Quality implications: Lossless target output (KL = 0) because every drafted token is verified by the target model on the next verification step; 97.1%..98.8% top-k index overlap, 0.999975..0.999986 3-layer DSpark output cosine similarity, and 95.8%..100.0% (98.5% mean) greedy Markov top-1 draft token agreement across 4K..256K.
Tests: pytest tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_dspark_topk_reuse.py tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_attention.py
Upstream status: Local optimization for DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash DSpark speculative decoding.
